    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_f70cd61981f21af74dad8e5fa18f8eeed107dd96908ce54b0f8c78adf2c791aa",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "A finite-sum logarithmic inequality, the chi-factor asymptotics from Lemma 1, and the definition of J_m reduce the boundary logarithm to a finite family of fractional moments of zeta^(j)/zeta. The reduction replaces a nonlinear differential sum by estimable ratio moments, at the cost of inequality loss, and leaves the actual moment bound to the next claim.",
