    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1fbf43804c40e9c3bdf0c878bc65ed08479c2d9d5bc44c90b57c540e538bc88d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A normalized combination of the completed zeta function and its derivative distinguishes simple zeros from multiplicity loss. Symmetry, Littlewood's lemma, and Jensen convert the resulting auxiliary-zero mass into a bound on the distinct-zero deficit; rewriting the detector as an affine differential polynomial in zeta makes Conrey's mollified mean-square theorem applicable, and a reported parameter choice supplies the numerical lower-bound certificate.",
