      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b9875d87f9bad98e577ed6ee6aaaf96b923a0829038de8a708f0172e06708d90",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Two related decompositions isolate the derivative-zero contributions on opposite sides: the common horizontal-displacement statistic lets the comparison theorem transfer Selberg's one-sided zeta-zero bound to a derivative-zero bound, while subtracting that bounded derivative-zero side from an imported total first-moment formula yields the complementary derivative-zero asymptotic.",
