    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_bdd2edce80d79b39b595e0dea411ca4d86e98998017b96316077fa0680deb5de",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Littlewood's lemma and Jensen turn a complementary one-sided derivative-zero count into an upper bound through the mollified L2 mean of J_k. A differential-polynomial proxy V_k places that mean under Conrey's theorem, after which a hyperbolic-sine trial profile and a balancing choice bound the variational constant; comparison with the total derivative-zero count converts the bound into the stated positive-proportion result.",
